      "writtenOn": "2026-07-10T16:49:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we want to expose this init call publicly. Like we don\u0027t want clients to make this call. Instead I think we just want to call it every time we create a new SkContext. So in that case it could either be private in this class or just make it a helper function in the cpp file.\n\nNow the initial reaction to call it when we create a new SkContext would be to call it in the ctor. This is probably safe and okay, the only caveat is if any of the context factories would ever need to know/use the stuff that is initialized here. If so, we\u0027d need to call this at the start of every factory function. I would ask Kaylee if she has any better insights here onto the right timing to call it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 87,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "226ae16f3d87b523fd95d230fdb06f8433e7d198",
