      "writtenOn": "2026-07-10T16:49:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You should just be declaring the member variables in the header and not initializing them. The initialization should happen in the constructor.\n\nAdditionally since these are member variables and not longer just globals, we can\u0027t just store raw pointers and assume they get cleaned up when the process goes away. We are responsible for freeing the allocated memory when the SkContext goes away. Thus we should wrap these in something like std::unique_ptr to auto delete them when the SkContext is destroyed.",
